msgid "freeports\\_dev.repo\\_init"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init:1 of
msgid ""
"Initialize a new freeports repository skeleton — a formats repository or "
"an input database."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init:3 of
msgid ""
"The two are different things and are used by different people, but they "
"are bootstrapped the same way: a list of directories, a set of files that"
" are nothing but their header row, a manifest, and an optional git "
"repository around them. So they share the readers below, and each entry "
"point differs only in which data files under lib/ it names."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init:8 of
msgid ""
"Reads template files from the adjacent lib/ directory so content can be "
"modified without touching Python code."
msgstr ""

