msgid "Create a new input database skeleton at `target`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/generated/modules/freeports_dev.repo_init.rst
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init.init_format_repo:3 of
msgid ""
"Path to the new repository directory. Must be empty or non-existent (a "
".git directory is tolerated)."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init.init_format_repo:6
#: freeports_dev.repo_init.init_input_db:18 of
msgid "If True, skip interactive prompts (defaults to yes for git init)."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init.init_input_db:3 of
msgid ""
"What comes out is an empty but *complete* database: all seven tables the "
"engine reads exist and carry their header row. That completeness is the "
"point — the loader requires every one of them, so a skeleton missing the "
"file you have nothing to put in yet would fail on the first run for a "
"reason that has nothing to do with what you were doing."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init.init_input_db:8 of
msgid ""
"It gets a `.githooks/pre-commit` of its own, which it did not use to. A "
"database has no test suite, so the hook checks the one thing a database "
"can be wrong about on its own terms: that the fingerprints in "
"`metadata.yaml` and the version it declares moved together."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init.init_input_db:12 of
msgid ""
"Path to the new database directory. Must be empty or non-existent (a .git"
" directory is tolerated)."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.repo_init.init_input_db:15 of
msgid ""
"If True, overwrite the empty tables with the packaged example database — "
"the single list `TEST` and the few hundred companies in it — as a "
"starting point to edit down."
msgstr ""

